<!--
  <sui-collapsible> — SUI port of <ship-collapsible>.
  Native disclosure: a <details>/<summary> pair. The open/close toggle,
  keyboard activation (Enter/Space on the trigger), and the ARIA
  expanded-state exposure are the browser's now — none of that is
  hand-rolled JS anymore.

  Prop parity vs <ship-collapsible>
  ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Lit                          SUI                      Notes
  ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  open (bool, false)           open (bool, reflect)     ✓
  disabled (bool, false)       disabled (bool, reflect) ✓ LANG-GAP below
  ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  ship-toggle → {open: bool}   sui-toggle → {open:bool} event renamed
  ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  slots: trigger               trigger                  ✓ now rendered inside
                                                          <summary>
         (default) content     (default) content        ✓
  ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  parts: content               part="content"           ✓ the content-wrap div
  ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  ARIA: aria-expanded +        native <details>/         ✓ browser-owned; no
    aria-controls on trigger    <summary> semantics        explicit aria-* set
    elements; tabindex=0 for
    non-focusable triggers
  keyboard: Enter/Space        native <summary>          ✓ browser-owned
    on trigger-wrap              activation behavior
  ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  animation: grid-template-    LANG-GAP — see below       ✗ dropped, see below
    rows 0fr→1fr; respects
    prefers-reduced-motion
  ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

  NATIVE REBUILD (native-rebuild-gate pass)
  ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  - <summary> IS the trigger-wrap now; the consumer's `slot="trigger"`
    content (a <button>, a <div>, whatever) renders inside it. <summary>
    is unconditionally focusable/keyboard-activatable per the HTML spec,
    so the old manual tabindex=0-for-non-interactive-triggers and the
    Enter/Space keydown handler are both DELETED — the browser does this
    for free now.
  - LANG-GAP: native <details> has no `disabled` concept. A click (or
    Enter/Space) on <summary> always toggles natively. The controller
    keeps a small capture-phase click/keydown listener that calls
    preventDefault() when the `disabled` prop is set, which suppresses
    the browser's native toggle. This is the one bit of JS native HTML
    cannot express — everything else (open/close, focus, ARIA) is gone.
  - LANG-GAP: the animated open/close (grid-template-rows 0fr→1fr) is
    DROPPED. Native <details> shows/hides its non-summary children via
    an internal UA behavior (not an overridable `display:none` rule at
    normal specificity in every engine), so the old grid-rows trick no
    longer has a reliable hook to animate against — the content is
    either fully in the accessibility/layout tree (open) or fully
    removed (closed), with no animatable intermediate state. The
    `::details-content` pseudo-element (Chrome 131+) can restore this
    but has no cross-browser support yet; flagged for the operator to
    decide whether to spend a progressive-enhancement pass on it.
    Toggling is now instant, no transition.
  - `display:block`/`color`/`[hidden]` on :host — framework-owned
    (BASE_CSS), same as before.
-->

<component>{
  props: {
    open: bool,
    disabled: bool,
  },
}</component>

<style>
  :host {
    font-family: var(--font-body);
  }

  summary.trigger-wrap {
    list-style: none;
    cursor: pointer;
    user-select: none;
    -webkit-user-select: none;
    transition: background var(--duration-fast) var(--ease-out);
  }
  summary.trigger-wrap::-webkit-details-marker { display: none; }
  summary.trigger-wrap::marker { content: ''; }
  summary.trigger-wrap:hover { background: var(--hover-bg); }
  summary.trigger-wrap:focus-visible {
    outline: var(--focus-ring);
    outline-offset: var(--focus-ring-offset);
  }
  :host([disabled]) summary.trigger-wrap {
    cursor: not-allowed;
    opacity: 0.5;
  }

  .content-inner { padding: 0; }
</style>

<details bind:this={detailsEl}>
  <summary class="trigger-wrap" bind:this={triggerWrap}>
    <slot name="trigger"></slot>
  </summary>
  <div class="content-wrap" part="content" bind:this={contentWrap}>
    <div class="content-inner">
      <slot></slot>
    </div>
  </div>
</details>
